  "id": "turkish_five_composers",
  "name": "Türk Beşleri (Turkish Five national-school art music)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Art music of the Turkish Five, Ahmed Adnan Saygun, Ulvi Cemal Erkin, Cemal Reşit Rey, Necil Kazım Akses and Hasan Ferit Alnar, composers born in the first decade of the twentieth century who answered the early Republic's call for a national art music by setting Anatolian folk modes and aksak rhythms in Western orchestral, chamber, choral and operatic forms. Most trained in Paris, Vienna or Prague, and Saygun accompanied Béla Bartók on his folk-song collecting trip in Anatolia. The string-orchestra card stands in for the orchestra's violin sections.",
  "recipe": "classic modern türk beşleri, art Music, western modern branch. solo and ensemble bowed string orchestra obbligato violin, norway spruce European alpine European maple general oil varnish amber tinted viola classical, norway spruce European alpine European maple sycamore maple oil varnish cello, norway spruce European alpine European maple sycamore maple oil varnish double bass, grenadilla African blackwood traditional clarinet, french horn, synthetic mallets timpani. shoebox concert hall. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
